Package: libpam-mfa-keyring
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         libpam-runtime,
         libpam-gnome-keyring,
         opensc-pkcs11
Recommends: mfa-keyring, sssd
Suggests: libpam-u2f
Description: unlock the GNOME keyring after smartcard or security key login
 PAM module that unlocks the GNOME login keyring when you log in to GDM with
 a PIV smartcard (through SSSD), passwordlessly with a FIDO2 security key
 (through pam_u2f), or with your password.
 .
 The keyring is protected by a random 256-bit secret, kept in a per-user file
 sealed separately to a PIV card key (decrypted on the card with your PIN), to
 a FIDO2 security key (hmac-secret extension) and to your login password
 (Argon2id).
 .
 Installs a gdm-smartcard PAM stack as the preferred alternative and a
 pam-auth-update profile.  Enrol with mfa-keyring.

Package: mfa-keyring
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         opensc-pkcs11,
         gnome-keyring
Recommends: libpam-mfa-keyring
Description: enrol PIV smartcards and FIDO2 keys to unlock the GNOME keyring
 Command line tool to enrol PIV smartcard keys, FIDO2 security keys and the
 login password as ways to unlock the GNOME login keyring.  It re-keys the
 login keyring to a random secret and writes the wrap file that
 pam_mfa_keyring uses at login.
